//
// WHY THIS PAGE IS DELIBERATELY NOT SHAPED LIKE A PIONEER PAGE.
//
// 1. THERE IS NO FIRMWARE. Not "none published": none at all. No firmware, no
//    drivers, no release notes, and no USB audio to need any. So the question
//    this whole site asks a Pioneer owner, "what version is the deck on", does
//    not exist here. The "Known issues" group therefore explains an ABSENCE,
//    and it explains it both ways: nothing to update before a gig, and equally
//    no fix coming for anything you do not like, because it is all hardware.
//    There is no "known issues by firmware version" section and there must
//    never be one on this model.
//
// 2. THE USER GUIDE HAS NO TROUBLESHOOTING SECTION. Checked. That is a fair,
//    checkable statement about the documentation rather than a dig, and it is
//    most of why this page is worth writing at all.
//
